== 1. a scope disposes what it built, newest first ==
ok   construction order: +a +b +c +p
ok   disposal order, and Plain silently skipped: -c -b -a

== 2. a second scope builds and closes its own ==
ok   a scope builds only what it is asked for: +a +b
ok   and closes only those: -b -a

== 3. a transient is handed over, not held ==
ok   two transients built: +f +f
ok   and the scope disposes neither — it kept no reference: 

== 4. a singleton outlives every scope ==
ok   built once, on first use: +pool
ok   closing a scope does NOT dispose it: 
ok   a later scope gets the same one, unbuilt: 
ok   closing the root disposes it: -pool
ok   exactly once: 1
